**Localization:** PC11 (172.16.20.11/24, eth0 UP) has the correct IP address, subnet mask, and default gateway (172.16.20.254, resolved in ARP). Live pings from PC11 to both same-subnet VLAN 20 neighbors — PC9 (172.16.20.9) and PC10 (172.16.20.10) — return 0% loss at sub-millisecond RTT. Cross-subnet reachability to 10.5.0.x targets also shows 0% loss. Interface counters carry zero errors, drops, or carrier events; only startup-time tap-rename and bridge-init entries appear in dmesg; no flap script or stress process is running on the host.

**Infrastructure sweep:** infra_sweep confirmed all 15 hosts have valid IPv4 addresses and default routes with no resolver or gateway divergence. l2_snapshot found no duplicate MACs. The OSPF fabric spanning all nine routers is fully converged (18 routes on every router, all adjacencies Full). No TC shaping or ACL drop rules were found on any device. Pressure sweep returned zero suspect devices.

**Root cause:** No anomaly exists. The user's complaint likely describes a transient or already-resolved condition; there is no injected fault, misconfiguration, or failure mechanism present in the current lab state.

**Fix:** No corrective action required. If the user experiences renewed issues, collect the symptom in real time (e.g., a failing ping from the user's desk) and re-run diagnostics at that moment.
